{
 "id": "BG-PID-02-close-gone-records",
 "note": "A live probe of background sessions showed that a background session the supervisor moved to a new version fires no SessionEnd in the old process, only SessionStart resume in the new one, so the old live- record stayed with no ended- twin. When the session starts again, each of its own live- records of this host whose process is gone (no such pid, or another start time) gets the twin, reason gone. A running process with its start time, a record of another host or with no host, a record already ended, this process's own record and another session's record are left as they are; no live- record is removed. The case clock sits an hour after the records (0.1.4: a session's records of ended processes over a week old are pruned once a day; lib/sessions.pm prune_records, V014-VS-14)",
